{
  "version": 1,
  "contract": "SMS text = base64(0x02 | mode | payload). mode 0x00 clear: payload = codec | body. mode 0x01 AES-256-GCM: payload = nonce(12) | ciphertext(codec | body) | tag(16), no AAD. codec 0x00 UTF-8 text, 0x01 SMAZ2 with the default table, 0x02 MSVQ-SC. Senders: MSVQ-SC when set and it encodes, else SMAZ2 when shorter, else the text. A plain SMS (no key, no compression) is the typed text, unframed.",
  "kept": "status kept: the receiver shows the SMS text as it came (the base64), reads nothing into it, and logs the unknown mode or codec. status legacy: version 1 or unversioned, read by the old rule; its ambiguity is the contract's reason to exist.",
  "key_hex": "101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f202122232425262728292a2b2c2d2e2f",
